# Source hygiene for the .NET 8 (net8.0) solution in this repository.
#
# This file excludes GENERATED build output and per-developer editor state only. Every
# hand-authored file stays tracked: LegacyPort.sln, global.json, Directory.Build.props,
# Directory.Packages.props, .editorconfig, .dockerignore, Dockerfile, README.md,
# .github/workflows/ci.yml, and every *.cs and *.csproj under src/ and tests/.
# Never add a broad pattern such as *.json, *.props, *.sln, *.yml, *.config or .* - each
# would hide one of those files. Ignoring global.json in particular would silently break
# the SDK pin that makes this build reproducible.
#
# The Docker build context is filtered separately by .dockerignore, which has a different
# consumer and therefore a different (partly overlapping) list. Neither file substitutes
# for the other, and .github/ is excluded from the image context there - never here.

# Build output. MSBuild writes each project to bin/<Configuration>/net8.0/ and keeps its
# intermediate output, including the NuGet restore assets, under obj/.
bin/
obj/

# Test and coverage output. The CI workflow writes its .trx to ./artifacts/test-results;
# a local `dotnet test` without --results-directory writes to <project>/TestResults/.
artifacts/
[Tt]est[Rr]esults/
*.trx
[Cc]overage*/
*.coverage
*.coverlet.json

# IDE and editor state. Per-developer, machine-specific, never shared.
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.user
*.suo
*.userprefs
*.DotSettings.user

# NuGet package output. Nothing in this repository is packed for publication, so any
# package file present locally is a build by-product.
*.nupkg
*.snupkg

# Operating-system and editor scratch files.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
